<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Whip</h1>
<p>Average Length: 6 feet.
Type of weapon: Distanced Hand-to-Hand.
Commonly used by: Many classes.
</p><p>This was not a typical weapon, but it was fairly easy to come by. It was really a decent weapon, and could be used in a variety of ways (whipping, disabling an arm or leg, grabbing weapons, or as a rope). It could be cut easily by a sword, and it was hard to judge the distance for a snap while moving around, but it was pretty useful.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the whip is a weapon skill of its own, one of the special weapons (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it slashes, it leans on dexterity, with some strength, and it is quick, as light weapons are. It is taught by the fighters from guild level 0 (up to 80%), the thieves from guild level 8 (up to 80%), the knights from guild level 9 and the paladins from guild level 9.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
